      "track": "section-b",
      "title": "Question 1 · C function",
      "markdown": "A Hamming number is a positive integer with no prime factors other than 2, 3 or 5.\n\nFor example, 12 (2 × 2 × 3) is a Hamming number while 14 (2 × 7) is not.",
      "displayCode": {
        "c": "int hamming(int n){\n   int i;\n   if (n == 1)\n      return 1;\n   i = 0;\n   if (n % 2 == 0)\n      i = 2;\n   if (n % 3 == 0)\n      i = 3;\n   if (n % 5 == 0)\n      i = 5;\n   if (i == 0)\n      {{A}};\n   else\n      {{B}};\n}"
      }
    }
  ],
